WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040
Wednesday, halfway through the trading week. Welcome to modern investing techniques Episode 93.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:12.100
It's July 1st, 2026, and I'm Patrick in Vancouver. Midweek, let's reassess this week's

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:17.680
positions and look for fresh setups. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:23.700
and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:29.960
I'm not a licensed financial advisor, and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:36.380
before putting real money to work. International Tech's first half outperformance gives Canadian TFS

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:44.200
A holders a concrete reason to add global equity exposure beyond US names. The S&amp;P 500 closed

00:00:44.200 --> 00:01:01.220
at 7,499, up 0.8%. The NASDAQ composite closed at 26,214, up 1.5%. The TSX composite closed at 34,857,

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:11.080
up 0.1%. Non-US tech names led first half gains while US big tech lagged. Gold posted its worst quarter

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:18.380
in 13 years, oil prices moved on shifting US Iran talks. The Bank of Canada rate decision

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:24.680
sits in the fall. Sector rotation into international equities works by systematically overweighting

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:30.840
regions showing relative strength rather than chasing single country mega caps. Today's data shows

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:37.140
US big tech delivered solid but not leading returns while emerging market and non-US tech names

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:43.660
outperformed creating a measurable spread. Canadian investors can implement this by allocating a sleeve

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:51.680
of their TFSA to a broad international ETF such as XEF or VIU and rebalancing quarterly against

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:58.080
the NASDAQ composite. The approach has historically delivered excess returns during periods when US

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:04.660
valuations stretched and global earnings revisions turned positive. Risks include currency translation

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:11.020
losses and delayed reaction when US names re-accelerate. The key metric to watch is the rolling

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:19.800
three-month relative performance of the MSCI ACWI XUSA versus the NASDAQ. This is the exact scenario

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:25.300
where our earlier rule about closing price confirmation would have helped avoid chasing headline

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:31.700
strength alone. Our practice investment of the day is a simulated weekly hold on general mills.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:40.360
The ticker is GIS on the NYSE in the consumer sector. General mills beat estimates by 14 cents with

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:46.120
revenue topping consensus. That provides a fundamental anchor in a soft consumer environment.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:51.500
Entry is considered only after a positive close to satisfied confirmation rules.

00:02:52.180 --> 00:03:00.020
The initial stop sits 6% below entry. The target is plus 2% to plus 5% over the five day window if

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:06.120
follow through buying appears. This is a medium confidence setup because it rests on a single earnings

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:12.380
catalyst without volume or technical confirmation yet. This trade demonstrates how to evaluate and

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:17.760
earnings beat as a potential entry while respecting the requirement for closing price confirmation

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:26.740
before treating the catalyst as complete. Yesterday's flash trade on MU entered at $1,233 at market open

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:40.440
and exited at $1,213.56 at market close. The position lost 1.58% or $15.77 on a $1,000 simulated stake.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:48.420
The NASDAQ rose 1.5% the same day, producing negative 3.08% alpha on that trade.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:55.220
The single day momentum entry reversed without follow through. This reinforces that earnings revision

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:59.460
signals need sustained price action rather than opening strength alone.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:05.500
The rule now in effect is to require closing price confirmation before declaring any catalyst

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:12.000
trade complete. Bloomberg Wealth Advisors outline a repeatable process for deploying a six-figure

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:18.200
windfall across asset classes using current valuations and risk budgets. Canadian listeners can

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:24.820
adapt the same framework inside a TFSA by mapping the recommended equity, fixed income, and alternative

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:31.740
buckets to available ETFs. The edge comes from forcing explicit position sizing before market moves

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:38.140
rather than reacting after the fact. The Bank of Canada quarterly survey aggregates views from

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:44.600
financial freelance market participants on growth, inflation, and policy expectations. Investors

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:50.260
can layer these consensus ranges into macro regime screens to adjust sector weights ahead of

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:56.460
Bank of Canada decisions. The raw results are released on the Bank of Canada website at 1030

00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:03.800
ET on survey dates. Service now jumped 4% after Guggenheim flipped from neutral to buy on strong

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:09.400
software fundamentals. The upgrade came from a firm that had previously maintained a neutral

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:15.220
stance on the name. Strong software fundamentals supported the immediate price response following

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:21.500
the rating change. Listeners tracking enterprise software names saw the move play out in real time

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:28.600
on the trading day. Adding now to the TFSA watch list allows monitoring without immediate commitment.

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:34.880
Waiting for a closing price above the upgrade day high provides a confirmation step before any

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:43.040
entry consideration. The source for this analyst action is investing.com. Qualis stock surged 65%

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:48.820
after an investing pro fair value signal triggered a sharp re-rating on the cybersecurity name.

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:54.380
The fair value model produced a clear re-rating signal that drove the outsized move.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:06:00.720
Cybersecurity peers provide a useful benchmark for assessing whether the new valuation level holds.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:06.740
Reviewing Qualis valuation metrics against those peers helps determine if the surge reflects

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:12.600
sustainable fundamentals. The surge occurred on the day the investing pro signal was highlighted

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:18.620
in market coverage. No immediate portfolio addition is required until the valuation review is

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:25.140
complete. Gold prices declined after logging their worst quarter in 13 years. The quarterly

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:30.880
performance marked the weakest stretch for the metal in that time frame. Precious metals exposure

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:42.580
therefore faces continued pressure from the sharp drop. Portfolio holders with gold or gold

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:48.880
any allocation that exceeds 5% of total portfolio reduces concentration risk if support breaks.

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:54.120
The move also affects broader commodity allocations that include precious metals.

00:06:54.880 --> 00:07:01.180
The source for this price action is investing.com. Demand for riskier mortgages dropped as the spread

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:07.540
between 30 year fixed and ARM's narrowed. The narrowing spread reduced the incentive for adjustable

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:14.100
rate products among borrowers. Canadian investors watching housing related assets saw this shift limit

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:20.800
the appeal of certain mortgage products. Holding CAD cash or short duration fixed income provides

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:27.200
a defensive stance during this period. Rotating into Canadian REITs is not favored this week given

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:33.520
the reduced demand dynamics. The change in mortgage preferences reflects broader interest rate environment

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:43.100
effects. The source for this trend is CNBC.com. The simulated portfolio now stands at $263.15

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:52.540
across 41 trades. The win rate sits at 51% with 21 wins. Cumulative alpha versus the NASDAQ reaches

00:07:52.540 --> 00:08:03.360
plus 11.0% across 30 benchmarked trades. Average return per trade is plus 0.64%. Our AI analysis

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:08.660
continues to adjust position sizing based on the pattern of single factor stories needing price

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:15.680
confirmation. Imagine you bought a mid cap Canadian name in your TFSA yesterday morning on a positive

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:23.080
headline. Your market order filled at $18.45. Between the moment you clicked and the fill,

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:29.480
the bid asked spread on that name widened from 3 cents to 14 cents because two market makers stepped

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:36.620
away during the first 20 minutes of trading. Quoted size at the inside bid dropped from 1,200 shares

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:43.060
to 300 while ask size stayed thin. So your order walked the book and paid the wider spread.

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:49.380
The effective spread can be measured in real time on most platforms by comparing the mid price to

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:55.780
the actual execution price. The professionals always check level 2 depth and average daily volume

00:08:55.780 --> 00:09:02.540
before entering anything under 500,000 shares ADV. The biggest mistake with spread risk is

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:08.840
assuming the posted quote will still be there when your order arrives. Instead, always use a limit order

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:14.880
set no more than one tick inside the current ask on names below 1 million shares ADV.

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:21.460
Before we wrap, open your brokerage screener, filter for consumer staples names that beat earnings by

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:28.340
at least 10% in the most recent quarter. Then sort by 5-day relative performance versus the TSX

00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:34.560
and note the top 3 for potential Monday entries. That wraps up today's modern investing techniques.

